{"created": "2026-05-28T15:36:21.672433+00:00", "modified": "2026-05-28T15:36:21.904579+00:00", "id": 20431754, "conceptrecid": "20431753", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20431754", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20431753", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20431754", "metadata": {"title": "Active Stabilizers In Reed\u2013Muller CSS Codes From Cayley\u2013Dickson Zero-Divisors", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20431754", "publication_date": "2026-05-28", "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\">We establish three results connecting the zero-divisor structure of the Cayley&ndash;Dickson algebras A\u2099 to the stabilizer formalism of quantum error-correcting codes.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\"><strong>Step 1 (Bijection, n=4).</strong> The 7 lo-flats of ZD(4) &mdash; weight-4 subsets {a,b,c,d} &sub; {1,...,7} with a&oplus;b&oplus;c&oplus;d=0 &mdash; are in explicit bijection with the 7 non-identity elements of the X-stabilizer group of the Steane [[7,1,3]] code. All 7 lo-flats carry identical sign-parity pattern: &pi;(EE|FF)=&minus;1 (inactive), &pi;(EF\u2081)=&pi;(EF\u2082)=+1 (active).</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\"><strong>Step 2 (Operator translation).</strong> For every mixed flat F={i,j,8+k,8+l} in A\u2084, the algebraic identity &pi;_A&middot;&pi;_B&middot;&pi;_C=&minus;1 translates into the Clifford-group identity (Z_&alpha;Z_&beta;)(X_&alpha;X_&gamma;)(X_&beta;X_&gamma;) = &minus;Y_&alpha;Y_&beta;. The global phase &minus;1 is the precise Clifford avatar of &pi;_A&pi;_B&pi;_C=&minus;1. The operator &minus;Y_&alpha;Y_&beta; is a detectable error with full-group syndrome weight 2^(n&minus;2), proved for all n&ge;4 and verified on QPU.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\"><strong>Step 3 (Extension to n=5, verified on QPU).</strong> The 15 Fano planes of PG(3,F\u2082) are in explicit bijection with the 15 non-identity elements of the X-stabilizer group S_X &cong; (Z/2Z)\u2074 of the [[15,7,3]] code (4 generators, 2\u2074&minus;1=15 non-identity elements). The phase identity and syndrome formula extend to all n&ge;4 (Universal Phase Lemma). Syndrome structure verified on ibm_kingston (156-qubit QPU, job d8bm67ijki0s73aq6idg, 27 May 2026).</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\">The Type-A/Type-B criterion for Fano planes in PG(3,F\u2082) is resolved: a plane W is Type-B if and only if 8&isin;W or W={1,...,7}, where 8=(1,0,0,0)&isin;F\u2082\u2074 is the bridge element between A\u2083 and A\u2084 in the Cayley&ndash;Dickson tower.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\">All algebraic results are cited from the companion papers (doi:10.5281/zenodo.20315751, doi:10.5281/zenodo.20417859).<br>Every claim is labelled [VERIFIED], [THEOREM], or [OPEN] throughout.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Levratti, Giovanni", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0000-9804-3452"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "20431753"}}]}}, "title": "Active Stabilizers In Reed\u2013Muller CSS Codes From Cayley\u2013Dickson Zero-Divisors", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20431754", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20431754?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20431754", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20431754", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20431754", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431753", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20431753", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20431753", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20431753", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754:ACTIVE%20STABILIZERS%20IN%20REED%E2%80%93MULLER%20CSS%20CODES%20FROM%20CAYLEY%E2%80%93DICKSON%20ZERO-DIVISORS_v1.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754:ACTIVE%20STABILIZERS%20IN%20REED%E2%80%93MULLER%20CSS%20CODES%20FROM%20CAYLEY%E2%80%93DICKSON%20ZERO-DIVISORS_v1.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754:ACTIVE%20STABILIZERS%20IN%20REED%E2%80%93MULLER%20CSS%20CODES%20FROM%20CAYLEY%E2%80%93DICKSON%20ZERO-DIVISORS_v1.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754:ACTIVE%20STABILIZERS%20IN%20REED%E2%80%93MULLER%20CSS%20CODES%20FROM%20CAYLEY%E2%80%93DICKSON%20ZERO-DIVISORS_v1.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754:ACTIVE%20STABILIZERS%20IN%20REED%E2%80%93MULLER%20CSS%20CODES%20FROM%20CAYLEY%E2%80%93DICKSON%20ZERO-DIVISORS_v1.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20431754:ACTIVE%20STABILIZERS%20IN%20REED%E2%80%93MULLER%20CSS%20CODES%20FROM%20CAYLEY%E2%80%93DICKSON%20ZERO-DIVISORS_v1.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20431754/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20431754/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/rec